<title>ARGENTINA: U.S. soybean exports to total 24.4 mln T - Sparks.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean exports to total 24.4 mln T - Sparks.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean exports this season should total 24.4 million tonnes, of which 22.5 million tonnes have already been exported, Sparks Companies said Monday.</p>
<p>Brazilian soybean exports should total 6.4 million tonnes, mainly to be shipped by August, U.S. agricultural consultant Sparks Companies of Memphis, Tenn. added in a report released at a conference in Buenos Aires.  </p>
<p>Sparks said it expected 1996/97 Brazilian soybean output of 26.4 million tonnes, and Argentine output of 11.9 million tonnes. Both the Brazilian and the Argentine crops have been hit by drought and frosts at the beginning of April, it said.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
